## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time streaming paths, backpressure management, reconnection handling, and cross-service visibility in a realistic production-like setup.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time data ingestion over WebSocket
- Normalization to canonical schema
- Downstream fan-out via message bus with backpressure
- Burst load simulation, tick miss detection, and reconnection handling
- End-to-end latency SLA verification and audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Synthetic tick generator
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://tdp.example');
ws.onopen = () => {
  for (let i = 0; i < 100000; i++) {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ symbol: 'AAPL', price: 150 + Math.random(), ts: Date.now() }));
  }
};

// Verify end-to-end latency
const tickSent = Date.now();
ws.onmessage = (msg) => {
  const latency = Date.now() - JSON.parse(msg.data).sentAt;
  if (latency > SLA_THRESHOLD_MS) alert(`SLA breach: ${latency}ms`);
};

// Reconnection with missed-tick detection
ws.onclose = () => reconnect(lastSequenceId);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design end-to-end tests for multi-region, multi-tenant feature flags, covering UI, API, and background workers, with rapid toggling and race conditions. Demonstrates seeds, isolation strategies, and SLA verification.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flag precedence and propagation across layers
- Cross-region consistency (UI, API, workers)
- Concurrency, load testing, and idempotency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold for E2E feature-flag toggles
async function testFlagToggle(tenantId, flagKey, value) {
  await api.setFlag(tenantId, flagKey, value);
  await wait(50);
  const uiState = await ui.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  const workerState = await worker.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  if (uiState !== value || workerState !== value) throw new Error('Inconsistent state');
}
```

